{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794770848","published":"2026-11-15T19:27:55Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:35.909418900Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116304","CVE-2026-116306","CVE-2026-116307","CVE-2026-116309","CVE-2026-116314","CVE-2026-116315","CVE-2026-116316","CVE-2026-116317","CVE-2026-116319","CVE-2026-116320","CVE-2026-116323","CVE-2026-116326","CVE-2026-116330","CVE-2026-116331","CVE-2026-116332","CVE-2026-116335","CVE-2026-116336","CVE-2026-120139","CVE-2026-120141","CVE-2026-120143","CVE-2026-120145","CVE-2026-120147","CVE-2026-120150","CVE-2026-120151","CVE-2026-120153","CVE-2026-18447","CVE-2026-6460","CVE-2026-6467"],"summary":"postgresql: Fix of 28 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-116309: fix type confusion in PL/Perl's get_perl_array_ref()\n- CVE-2026-116326: support tied Perl objects in plperl and the hstore_plperl\n  and jsonb_plperl transforms, so tied values can no longer cause type\n  confusion\n- CVE-2026-116320: hold a reference on a Perl array or hash while scanning it,\n  avoiding use-after-free\n- CVE-2026-116319: plperl: do not save and re-use the temporary context in\n  return_next(), avoiding use-after-free\n- CVE-2026-116307: plperl: refuse to free a prepared query that is being\n  executed\n- CVE-2026-116304: fix possible use-after-free in\n  find_or_make_matching_shared_tupledesc()\n- CVE-2026-116306: handle composite type changes in\n  ExecEvalFieldStoreDeForm/Form\n- CVE-2026-116314: pg_restore: fix out-of-bounds accesses and path traversal\n- CVE-2026-116315: fix potential buffer overrun in tsvector_delete()\n- CVE-2026-116317: fix potential buffer overrun in ts_rank_cd()\n- CVE-2026-116323: avoid use-after-free hazards in re-entrant use of pltcl\n- CVE-2026-116330: make \\restrict keys protective in pg_dump --format=tar\n  restore.sql\n- CVE-2026-116331: do not use MinMaxAggPath if the aggregate's input and\n  output types differ\n- CVE-2026-116332: fix use-after-free due to drop of portals that are being\n  set up\n- CVE-2026-116335: check that commutator and negator operators return the same\n  data type\n- CVE-2026-120141: fix type confusion with materialized set-returning\n  functions\n- CVE-2026-120143: close portals at end of trigger functions with transition\n  tables\n- CVE-2026-120147: dblink: refuse to use a connection that a dblink call is\n  already using\n- CVE-2026-120150: avoid using a dangling pointer in expanded-record domain\n  checks\n- CVE-2026-120151: plpgsql: recheck a record field's type after casting the\n  value\n- CVE-2026-120153: reject more unsafe names in extension script substitutions\n- CVE-2026-6467: block the ALTER SCHEMA RENAME attack on CREATE EXTENSION via\n  locking\n- CVE-2026-18447: reject pseudo-type output parameters in SQL functions\n- CVE-2026-116316: prevent creating types in pg_temp from restricted code\n- CVE-2026-116336: fix crash in REINDEX CONCURRENTLY due to DDL run in index\n  functions\n- CVE-2026-120139: protect against miscalculation of tuple sizes via int32\n  overflow\n- CVE-2026-120145: reject system catalogs as logical replication targets\n- CVE-2026-6460: forbid ALTERing a column or composite type used by stored\n  expressions, defaults, constraints or indexes; fix related locking races\n  (partial mitigation)\n- Add BuildRequires: perl(FindBin), needed by genbki.pl","affected":[{"package":{"name":"postgresql","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/postgresql?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"13.23-1.el9_6.tuxcare.els17"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1794770848.json"}},{"package":{"name":"postgresql-contrib","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/postgresql-contrib?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"13.23-1.el9_6.tuxcare.els17"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/clou